  "b6_reason": "For a sinusoidal ac source the peak value is sqrt(2) times the rms value, which is option 3 once its lost square-root sign is restored.",
  "b6_working": "V_rms = V_peak / sqrt(2), so V_peak = sqrt(2) * V_rms ~= 1.414 V_rms. Option 4 (1/sqrt(2) times rms) is the inverse relation and option 2 (equal to rms) holds only for dc.",
  "b6_confidence": "medium",
  "b6_note": "Options 3 and 4 arrived with the square-root sign stripped ('2 times' and '1/ 2 times'). Read literally, option 3 says 2 x rms, which is not correct; the intended sqrt(2) x rms is the only correct statement in the set, so option 3 is the answer on the restored reading.",
